cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CryptoServe Census
message: >-
  Cite the dated dataset you used, not the repository. Each directory under
  datasets/ is an independent, immutable release with its own collection date.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: CryptoServe
    website: https://census.cryptoserve.dev
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/ecolibria/crypto-census-data
url: https://census.cryptoserve.dev
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21791658
    description: >-
      The 2026-08-03 dataset. Cite this one if that is the data you read.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21791657
    description: >-
      Concept DOI for the series. It resolves to the most recently deposited
      dataset, so it names the collection rather than the bytes.
abstract: >-
  Cryptographic dependency adoption across eleven public package registries.
  Each dataset records, per ecosystem, how many packages were listed for
  scanning and how many matched a catalogued cryptographic library, split
  across weak, modern and post-quantum tiers.
  The listed counts can include packages that could not be read, and they are
  not counts of packages using cryptography; every published share is over the
  subset that matched a catalogued library.
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - software supply chain
  - package registries
  - dependency analysis
